  "content": {
    "id": "p48-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Find the tangents and normals to these curves at the indicated points.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p48-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=x(1-x)^6$ at the origin.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Tangent: $y=x$.\n\nNormal: $y=-x$.",
          "worked": "Let $u=x$ and $v=(1-x)^6$. Then $u'=1$ and $v'=-6(1-x)^5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y'&=u'v+uv'\\\\&=(1-x)^6-6x(1-x)^5\\\\&=(1-x)^5(1-7x).\\end{align*}$$\nAt $(0,0)$, $m_T=1$ and $m_N=-1$.\n\nTangent:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-0&=1(x-0)\\\\y&=x.\\end{align*}$$\nNormal:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-0&=-1(x-0)\\\\y&=-x.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p48-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=(2x-1)^3(x-2)^4$ at $A(1,1)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Tangent: $y=2x-1$.\n\nNormal: $y=-\\dfrac{x}{2}+\\dfrac{3}{2}$.",
          "worked": "Let $u=(2x-1)^3$ and $v=(x-2)^4$. Then $u'=6(2x-1)^2$ and $v'=4(x-2)^3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y'&=u'v+uv'\\\\&=6(2x-1)^2(x-2)^4\\\\&\\quad+4(2x-1)^3(x-2)^3\\\\&=2(2x-1)^2(x-2)^3\\\\&\\quad\\times[3(x-2)+2(2x-1)]\\\\&=2(2x-1)^2(x-2)^3(7x-8).\\end{align*}$$\nAt $x=1$,\n$$m_T=2(1)^2(-1)^3(-1)=2.$$\nHence $m_N=-\\dfrac12$.\n\nTangent:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-1&=2(x-1)\\\\y&=2x-1.\\end{align*}$$\nNormal:\n$$\\begin{align*}y-1&=-\\frac12(x-1)\\\\y&=-\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac32.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 55
      }
    ]
